    "name": "clinic-conflict-a-named-attendee-who-rotates-nowhere",
    "why": "Design §14 item 22's formulation is unit-only — the person's rotation on the date against the clinic's unit — and this is the case it is wrong on in BOTH directions at once (P2 finding 17, owner decision S). p-zain rotates on no unit at all and is NAMED on the Tuesday clinic, so the unit-only reading reports nothing where the collision is real; the rotators-mode clinic on the same unit, the same weekday and the same session must NOT match them, so a reading that treats every mode as 'anybody on the unit' reports two collisions where there is one. `ClinicRoster::forDate()` resolves named attendees without consulting the rota at all, and this mirrors that rather than re-deciding it.",
